@startuml seq_flt_dtc_memory
title SC-FLT-08 - Fault memory: read and clear DTCs

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "UDS tester" as Tester
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-FLT-007, SYS-DIA-002, SYS-DIA-003, SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-008, SIM-TST-003, SIM-CON-003
UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9 (can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
DTC status bits: testFailed (bit 0, fault currently set), confirmedDTC (bit 3, set since the last clear);
availability mask 0x09; DTCFormatIdentifier 0x00 (can_matrix section 3.6).
end note

== fault sets its DTC ==
User -> Console : force LinePressVoltage = 0 mV (SIM-CON-003)
Console -> Plant : sensor voltage forced
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: LinePressVoltage = 0 mV
... longer than 100 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : line pressure sensor fault (FaultBits 4) -> limp-home (SC-FLT-04);\nDTC P0840-1C (08 40 1C): status 0x09 (SYS-FLT-007)

== read (default session, no security access) ==
Tester -> TCU : 19 01 09
TCU --> Tester : 59 01 09 00 00 01
note right: availability mask 09, format 00, one DTC
Tester -> TCU : 19 02 09
TCU --> Tester : 59 02 09 08 40 1C 09
Tester -> Tester : show P0840-1C line pressure sensor fault (SIM-TST-003)

== clear while the fault is still present ==
Tester -> TCU : 14 FF FF FF
TCU --> Tester : 54
TCU -> TCU : DTCs cleared; mode, fault bits and outputs unchanged,\nlimp-home stays (SYS-FLT-007, SYS-FLT-004)
TCU -> TCU : the fault is still present: DTC P0840-1C set again, status 0x09
Tester -> TCU : 19 02 09
TCU --> Tester : 59 02 09 08 40 1C 09

opt DTC setting off (85 02)
  Tester -> TCU : 10 03
  TCU --> Tester : 50 03 00 32 01 F4
  note right: P2 = 50 ms, P2* = 5000 ms (10 ms units)
  Tester -> TCU : 85 02
  TCU --> Tester : C5 02
  User -> Console : force OilTempVoltage = 0 mV
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: OilTempVoltage = 0 mV
  ... longer than 100 ms ...
  TCU -> TCU : oil temperature sensor fault (FaultBits 5 = 1);\nDTC status bits not updated while DTC setting is off (SYS-FLT-007)
  Tester -> TCU : 19 02 09
  TCU --> Tester : 59 02 09 08 40 1C 09
  note right: P0710-1C not reported
  ... no request for S3 = 5000 ms ...
  TCU -> TCU : default session, effect of 85 undone (SYS-DIA-003):\nDTC P0710-1C set, status 0x09
end

== power cycle ==
User -> Console : remove all injections
TCU -> TCU : reset: volatile DTC memory cleared (SYS-FLT-007),\nlimp-home and fault bits cleared (SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-008)
Tester -> TCU : 19 02 09
TCU --> Tester : 59 02 09
note right: no DTC stored
@enduml
